From 729b7d6b9f9b89bbd6a13a16e0717eb4cbb5cbb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 09:50:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0056 -- silence-detect runtime killswitch
 (default-ON)

Adds SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_DETECT runtime killswitch for SDL/0054
Shape A post-mix silence-detect. Default-ON (silence-detect enabled;
SFX-correct path; pays the wave-35 +3.34 ms fi_ms slice cost). Set
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_DETECT=0 to disable (skip silence-scan +
skip-ring-write branch in PlayDevice; reverts to wave-34 always-fill-ring
behavior; SFX silent under AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3 because Pixtone never
propagates -- the wave-34 known-broken-but-fast path, exposed here for
perf-experiment A/B isolation only).

Implementation:

  - New module-scope static bool g_dos_silence_detect_enabled, default
    true. Distinct from g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled (which
    carries the older SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE
    semantic AND doubles as SDL/0053's engine-signaled shutdown gate
    via SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown). Per
    sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md, adding a separate
    flag avoids the state-flag-fragmentation footgun -- the new
    user-facing perf killswitch does not entangle with the shutdown
    coordination contract.

  - OpenDevice reads SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_DETECT once via
    SDL_GetHint (strict-"0" match per CLAUDE.md env-var convention:
    only literal "0" disables; unset/empty/"1"/anything else enabled).
    Cached at module scope; read by PlayDevice in the hot path.

  - PlayDevice silence-scan block now runs iff BOTH:
        g_dos_silence_detect_enabled               (this patch)
      && !g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled    (SDL/0050/0053/0054)

  - Boot banner emits one of two essential variants for decomp
    engagement-verify (so the operator BAT cell that sets =0 can be
    confirmed to actually engage the disabled path before attributing
    fps delta to silence-detect cost):

      default-ON:  "audio: SDL/0054 silence-detect ACTIVE
                    (default; SFX-correct)"
      SET=0:       "audio: SDL/0054 silence-detect DISABLED
                    (env-var; perf-experiment)"

Why this ships now (wave-36, not WITH SDL/0054 at wave-35):

  Per correctness_vs_perf_trade_machinery_at_authoring.md, this is the
  canonical example of a correctness-vs-perf-trade killswitch that
  should have shipped with the correctness patch. SDL/0054 (silent-SFX
  fix; Shape A post-mix silence-scan) landed wave-35 default-ON without
  a runtime A/B mechanism. Wave-35 then measured an unexpected -5.96 fps
  regression (W34A1 41.67 -> W35A1 35.71) attributable to +3.34 ms fi_ms
  per-flip slice, and the cost was not A/B-able in the same iter. This
  patch provides the missing A/B switch so wave-36 can isolate the
  silence-detect contribution from the rest of the post-W34 deltas.

  Future-proofing: SDL/0057+ may ship a cheaper silence-detect shape
  (Shape B/C/D investigation underway; see wave-36 plan). If a cheaper
  shape lands default-ON, the same killswitch still applies (the
  bracket condition gates whatever silence-detect mechanism is wired up
  at the time).

User docs: docs/BOOT.md edit lands alongside this patch, categorized as
perf-experiment opt-out (NOT daily-use); operator should NEVER set
=0 in production sessions because SFX will be silent under the
default OPL3 music backend.

Validation:
  - Boot-banner strings verified in libSDL3.a via
    `strings build/sysroot/lib/libSDL3.a | grep silence-detect`
  - PlayDevice condition change is 1 line (single AND clause added);
    behavioral semantics unchanged at default
    (g_dos_silence_detect_enabled=true), so wave-35 SFX-audibility +
    +3.34 ms cost retained as the default-ship behavior.

Per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md the patch stays workspace-local; not for
upstream.

Companion patches:
  SDL/0054 -- Shape A silent-Pixtone-SFX fix (the patch this gates;
              the silence-scan code path itself is unchanged here)
  SDL/0055 -- P12 SDL-side audio brackets (sits above this patch
              numerically; coexists trivially -- different state flags,
              different code paths)
  SDL/0053 -- SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown engine-signal (uses the OLDER
              g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled flag, untouched
              here; both flags must allow PlayDevice silence-scan)
  SDL/0050 -- DOS GetDeviceBuf quiescence gate (superseded mechanism;
              hint name SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE
              retained for user-facing compat; orthogonal to the
              new SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_DETECT)

Cross-reference:
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-35-FINDINGS.md (the -5.96 fps regression +
    +3.34 ms fi_ms slice attribution that this killswitch enables
    wave-36 to A/B-isolate)
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md (wave-36 PLAY cell matrix uses
    SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_DETECT=0 as one of the isolation arms)
  - memory/correctness_vs_perf_trade_machinery_at_authoring.md
  - memory/env_vars_document_in_user_docs.md (BOOT.md edit required)
  - memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md (rationale
    for the separate-flag-not-overloaded-flag decision)
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 67 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 65 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 22a5f5864..3d9b511fe 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -66,6 +66,41 @@ static Uint8 soundblaster_silence_value = 0;
    PLAY2 control measurement to isolate SDL/0050 effect within iter. */
 static bool g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled = false;
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0056): runtime killswitch for SDL/0054
+   Shape A post-mix silence-detect. Default true (silence-detect enabled
+   -- SFX-correct path, paying the wave-35 +3.34 ms fi_ms slice cost).
+   Set SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_DETECT=0 to disable silence-detect for
+   perf-experiment runs (skips the bytewise scan + skip-ring-write
+   branch in PlayDevice; reverts to wave-34 always-fill-ring behavior;
+   SFX will be silent under AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3 because Pixtone never
+   propagates -- this is the wave-34 known-broken-but-fast path,
+   provided here for fps-cost isolation only).
+
+   Per CLAUDE.md strict-"0" env-var convention: only literal "0"
+   disables; unset/empty/"1"/anything else leaves silence-detect
+   enabled. Resolved once at OpenDevice time; cached at module scope;
+   read by DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice in the hot path.
+
+   Distinct from g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled (above): that
+   flag carries the older SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE
+   semantic AND doubles as SDL/0053's engine-signaled shutdown gate
+   (SDL_DOSAudioBeginShutdown flips it true). Adding a separate flag
+   keeps the new user-facing perf-experiment switch from entangling
+   with the shutdown coordination contract, per
+   memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md
+   (state-flag-fragmentation footgun: avoid overloading a single flag
+   across user-facing perf, shutdown, and legacy-compat semantics).
+
+   PlayDevice silence-detect block runs iff BOTH flags allow it:
+     g_dos_silence_detect_enabled       (this flag; perf killswitch)
+     && !g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled  (shutdown + legacy)
+
+   correctness_vs_perf_trade_machinery_at_authoring.md: this killswitch
+   is the trade-machinery that should have shipped WITH SDL/0054; it
+   lands now as part of wave-36 perf decomp + 50-fps-with-SFX
+   stretch framing. */
+static bool g_dos_silence_detect_enabled = true;
+
 /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): Phase 12 SDL-side audio
    instrumentation state. Pairs with engine-side nx 0131 brackets for
    wave-36 PLAY5 audio cost attribution per
@@ -601,6 +636,26 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
         }
     }
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0056): resolve silence-detect
+       runtime killswitch once at OpenDevice time. Strict-"0" match per
+       CLAUDE.md env-var convention. Cached at module scope; read by
+       DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice in the hot path. Boot banner emit is
+       essential for wave-36 decomp engagement-verify (operator BAT
+       cell that sets =0 must produce the DISABLED variant in the log
+       so we can confirm the killswitch path actually engaged before
+       attributing the fps delta to silence-detect cost). */
+    {
+        const char *sd_hint = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_DETECT");
+        const bool sd_disabled =
+            (sd_hint && sd_hint[0] == '0' && sd_hint[1] == 0);
+        g_dos_silence_detect_enabled = !sd_disabled;
+        if (g_dos_silence_detect_enabled) {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0054 silence-detect ACTIVE (default; SFX-correct)");
+        } else {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0054 silence-detect DISABLED (env-var; perf-experiment)");
+        }
+    }
+
     /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): resolve P12 SDL-side audio
        instrumentation gates once at OpenDevice time. BOTH FLIP_INSTR
        AND P12_AUDIO_INSTR must be set to "1" (strict-"1" match) for
@@ -1186,8 +1241,16 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
 
        Latency: SFX-trigger-to-first-sample-on-ring <= one audio-thread-
        iter cycle (~10-12 ms). Same as the pre-SDL/0050 working SFX
-       path; no perceptible regression for game SFX. */
-    if (!g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled) {
+       path; no perceptible regression for game SFX.
+
+       SDL/0056 adds g_dos_silence_detect_enabled as a separate
+       user-facing perf killswitch (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_DETECT=0).
+       Block runs iff BOTH flags allow it; either flag suppresses the
+       silence-scan + skip-ring-write path. See module-level comment on
+       g_dos_silence_detect_enabled (above the static decl) for the
+       rationale on keeping the perf switch separate from the
+       legacy-compat / shutdown flag. */
+    if (g_dos_silence_detect_enabled && !g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled) {
         const Uint8 silence = soundblaster_silence_value;
         const Uint8 *p = buffer;
         const Uint8 *end = buffer + buffer_size;
-- 
